{"id": "EUVD-2026-103848", "enisaUuid": "06cd08ae-a94c-30df-b27f-3e76f299fe60", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: core: clear both ep_in and ep_out for non-ep0 control endpoints\n\nIn usb_enable_endpoint(), non-zero control endpoints (where\nusb_endpoint_xfer_control(&ep->desc) is true) populate both\ndev->ep_in[epnum] and dev->ep_out[epnum] with the same struct\nusb_host_endpoint pointer.\n\nHowever, usb_disable_endpoint() only clears either dev->ep_out[epnum] or\ndev->ep_in[epnum] depending on the direction bit of epaddr when\nreset_hardware is set, leaving the opposite direction's array slot\npointing to the disabled/freed endpoint.\n\nClear both dev->ep_out[epnum] and dev->ep_in[epnum] when disabling a\nnon-ep0 control endpoint with reset_hardware set, and update the\nfunction kerneldoc accordingly.\n\nTested in QEMU against Linux 7.3.0-rc3 using dummy_hcd and raw-gadget to\nenumerate a USB device with a non-zero control endpoint\n(bEndpointAddress 0x01, bmAttributes USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_CONTROL),\nverifying that both dev->ep_in[1] and dev->ep_out[1] are cleared when\nthe interface is disabled.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/198d74dcfa129523125f46a89479d3b446b17dbe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a9f61476b0e8002092a52ee8295edeeb0a28d1e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1da16c46b8d7101b74bc2d72a04e23cf5c7ddea1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c50413ecb662ea43c7f487632c8114721743a277", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e8baa78d872f2db440d8b9ded946ab8dceb89eb"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f752-7j6x-76w7", "CVE-2026-98763"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a6a044a-c181-368f-8eba-353b3dc99d5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "1d39800d-7550-309c-990f-ecb5af4464e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2f9809b6-c358-3c1c-a2bf-85d924d9722f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "3d216e41-932d-3c08-a6fc-0d583ff8dedf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <7a9f61476b0e8002092a52ee8295edeeb0a28d1e"}, {"id": "69696c85-d458-3795-a143-a85e66a32b97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "95552fb9-5008-3a61-ac51-77c2b983c5b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <c50413ecb662ea43c7f487632c8114721743a277"}, {"id": "a18b6d88-5e87-394a-930c-55147d6724bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "b0491e62-8bcd-3bb7-9dfd-02a06130168a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <1da16c46b8d7101b74bc2d72a04e23cf5c7ddea1"}, {"id": "c5225b27-169b-3305-b03a-3da59860c7d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <198d74dcfa129523125f46a89479d3b446b17dbe"}, {"id": "c5fedbae-d5b0-300d-8cfb-94c34225cf93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ccafd3a1-8f62-306e-908e-617c5d4f1da6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "df46d7b3-2d5f-3e94-ac98-5a77607cd339", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <0e8baa78d872f2db440d8b9ded946ab8dceb89eb"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3573e1cb-e908-3f05-96dc-a3561e4f5cdd", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}